# musicdata — the dynamic-music description and the transition rules.
#
# `ext_data/dms.dat` describes one level, `testmap`, with an explore piece, an
# action piece, and a boss piece, plus a second level that reaches the first
# through the "uses" keyword. Nothing here decodes an MP3: the scenario drives
# the snd_music state machine only, which is what DEC-57.3 leaves inside the
# byte gate.
cvar s_khz 22
init
beginreg
dumpstate after-init

# The parse. `testmap` has both an explore and an action piece, so dynamic music
# is available; `nolevel` has no entry at all.
musicdata testmap
musicsetname
musicdata nolevel
musicdata usesmap
musicsetname

# The file name each state plays. 0 explore, 1 action, 2 boss, 3 death, then the
# four action transitions and the four explore transitions.
musicdata testmap
musicfile 0
musicfile 1
musicfile 2
musicfile 3
musicfile 4
musicfile 5
musicfile 8
musicfile 9
musicfile 13

# The interruption rules across every pair that matters.
musicinterrupt 0 1
musicinterrupt 1 0
musicinterrupt 0 2
musicinterrupt 2 0
musicinterrupt 2 13
musicinterrupt 3 1
musicinterrupt 1 3
musicinterrupt 4 0
musicinterrupt 4 1
musicinterrupt 4 13

# The exit points. The explore piece exits at 8 seconds, the action piece at 6
# and 12. The epsilon is 0.3 seconds either way.
musictransition 0.000 0
musictransition 7.800 0
musictransition 8.000 0
musictransition 8.400 0
musictransition 6.100 1
musictransition 11.900 1
musictransition 12.000 1
musictransition 20.000 1
musictransition 5.000 2

# The random entry time. The explore piece has two markers, so consecutive calls
# never answer the same one twice running.
musicentrytime 0
musicentrytime 0
musicentrytime 0
musicentrytime 1
musicentrytime 2
shutdown
